tor pedal implementations.'],'numeric':[['quantity':'independent pedal-return springs','value':2,'unit':'count','operator':'required pair'],['quantity':'released pedal travel','value':0,'unit':'%','operator':'equals']],'checks':'Inspect two pedal springs and their independence from APPS internals. Disconnect each spring in turn and demonstrate the remaining spring returns the pedal to zero travel throughout the approved operating conditions.','source_refs':[['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.1:p001','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.1','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'000ad943f58404c03a2598f4bb743bff1d3b6e6848667f9b3c81033f97055bca','source_pages':[67]],['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.1:p002','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.1','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'bb767e228bb0dc1a8c9b317848836645f7d4a4de663dff4f05268272d55659b1','source_pages':[67]],['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.1:p003','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.1','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'809e6f5707b435d6a9c4a311983e7c8ad442b5b5712ad7a17cfab4390b858e58','source_pages':[67]]],'classification':'technical_design_and_verification','interpretation_status':'interpreted_candidate','coverage_status':'prepared_not_applied','verification_method':'inspection_review_and_fault_injection','verification_status':'not_verified','evidence_status':'not_available','compliance_status':'not_claimed','conditions_json':'["All accelerator pedal implementations."]','numeric_json':'[{"quantity":"independent pedal-return springs","value":2,"unit":"count","operator":"required pair"},{"quantity":"released pedal travel","value":0,"unit":"%","operator":"equals"}]','source_ids_json':'["FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.1:p001","FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.1:p002","FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.1:p003"]'],['id':'DD-04','title':'Independent APPS channels and distinguishable transfer functions','rules':['T.4.2.2','T.4.2.3'],'functions':['apps-input','apps-fault'],'owner':'driver-demand APPS channels A and B','statement':'Use at least two electrically separate APPS sensors; two separate sensors in one OEM housing are permitted. Channel gradients and/or offsets differ. Bias open inputs to zero pedal travel. Above ten percent pedal position, each sensor output differs from every other by at least ten percent. Opposite slopes do not excuse this separation requirement. Calibration into comparable pedal-travel values is an unresolved design obligation.','conditions':['This candidate selects two analogue channels. It does not select the optional three-sensor degraded mode.'],'numeric':[['quantity':'electrically separate APPS sensors','value':2,'unit':'count','operator':'>='],['quantity':'pedal-position condition','value':10,'unit':'%','operator':'>'],['quantity':'channel-output separation','value':10,'unit':'%','operator':'>=']],'checks':'Inspect electrical independence and bias circuitry. Measure raw transfer functions over pedal travel, demonstrate required separation and zero-travel open-input behavior, and review calibrated comparison to avoid confusing raw-channel separation with plausibility deviation.','source_refs':[['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.2:p001','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.2','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'b2eff51c0e278b2ae2f31d1aa5a0eadbf1ac22c329400e7ca60de9a0d00cac88','source_pages':[67]],['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.3:p001','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.3','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'c14498d75a0e58b407cf4a5ed769e70aaaeca5c392ae9098259fd70fb75a9496','source_pages':[67]],['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.3:p002','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.3','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'8b63eae93af0e7ce5fd74b7aadbe06decaba572b17165d28a439