 travel, sensor failures and wiring failures as APPS implausibility. If implausibility persists longer than one hundred milliseconds, stop all motor power immediately. In an EV, stopping power through the motor controller is sufficient; opening the shutdown circuit is not required by this APPS clause. Analogue open/short faults outside the actual operating range must be detected using pull-up/down circuitry. The example 0.5/4.5 V values are not adopted as universal design thresholds. Proposing a deviation threshold above ten percent requires the stated form justification and approval review.','conditions':['Analogue APPS candidate; actual sensor operating range remains unresolved.'],'numeric':[['quantity':'APPS calibrated deviation','value':10,'unit':'% pedal travel','operator':'>'],['quantity':'implausibility persistence','value':100,'unit':'ms','operator':'>'],['quantity':'illustrative analogue fault range','lower':0.5,'upper':4.5,'unit':'V','role':'source example only; not selected operating range']],'checks':'Fault-inject each open, short, out-of-range and channel-deviation condition. Check strict threshold and persistence boundaries and complete motor-power removal after qualification. Document actual ranges, bias response and any proposed larger deviation threshold approval.','source_refs':[['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.4:p001','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.4','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'64f0507b41fb31a8e5ab78c0f2b8b0f526a8894f7e1f90cb0b4fa3fdf590bb19','source_pages':[67]],['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.5:p001','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.5','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_text_sha256':'127187649360fd1441970eb367cb4d2335e0f74defcf15d42421080e1b6ef949','source_pages':[67]],['clause_id':'FSAE-2027-V1:T.4.2.5:p002','source_rule_id':'T.4.2.5','source_sha256':'f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e','source_tex